.TH SPTLRPC.GSSIAM_SERVER.GSSIAM_FLUSH 4 2026-06-18 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush, sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush \- flush entries
in the GSS IAM upcall cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush=" KEY
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush=-1"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 200 " | " --w-------
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Global security setting.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Present on server targets (gssiam_server) or if GSS is enabled (gssiam).
.TP
.B Default
.br
N/A (Write-only)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush
and
.B sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush
parameters allow userspace to flush entries in the GSS IAM
(Identity and Access Management) upcall caches on clients and on servers
(targets), respectively.
.PP
Writing
.B -1
to this parameter flushes all upcall cache entries on the client, and flushes
idle cache entries while marking active cache entries as expired on the server/target.
.PP
For the client-side cache
.RB ( sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush ),
writing any other integer value
.I KEY
will invalidate the mount token cache entry.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush
.B sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Flush all idle GSS IAM cache entries on the server:
.EX
.RB "server# " "lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush=-1"
sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush=-1
.EE
.PP
Flush all GSS IAM cache entries on the client:
.EX
.RB "client# " "lctl set_param sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush=-1"
sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush=-1
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B sptlrpc.gssiam.gssiam_flush
and
.B sptlrpc.gssiam_server.gssiam_flush
parameters are part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_17_56
